type: software

title: "Continuous Planar Isotropy and Euclidean Length: A Lean-Verified Characterization"

authors:
  - family-names: Odasso
    given-names: Alessandro

abstract: >-
  Lean 4/Mathlib formalization characterizing Euclidean length
  through continuous additive linear planar symmetries.

  For an arbitrary axially calibrated length function, the
  existence of a continuous additive linear action containing
  a primitive oriented quarter-turn and preserving that function
  is equivalent to the Euclidean length formula.

  The development extends the original conditional Pythagorean
  theorem formalization (v0.1.0). It includes an explicit
  converse model and counterexamples showing that finite
  quarter-turn symmetry alone is insufficient.

  The mathematical arguments and exposition were AI-generated
  or AI-assisted following a research question initiated by
  Alessandro Odasso. Lean and independent Comparator verification
  establish correctness under the stated hypotheses, not
  historical novelty or minimality of those hypotheses.

